To edit "*.java" files
-------------------------

- Install JDK, use Visual Studio Code, use "Extension Pack for Java" extension.

or:

- Get a copy of JDK without installation (from official Download pages, "x64 Compressed Archive" for Windows),
  use Visual Studio Code, use "Extension Pack for Java" extension, go to File, Preferences, Settings, 
  find and edit this settings:

  "java.jdt.ls.java.home": "path-to-JDK folder"

  For additional .jar files:

  "java.project.referencedLibraries": 
  [
    "path to xxx1.jar",
    "path to xxx2.jar"
  ]

- The new version of RE2J (.jar) can be got from https://github.com/google/re2j/releases.

- The new version of SafeRE (.jar) can be got from https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/org.safere/safere.

- The new version of Reggie (.jar) can be got from https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/com.datadoghq/reggie.

- The new version of Joni (.jar) can be got from https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/org.jruby.joni/joni.

To recompile the "*.java" workers
--------------------------------------------------------

- Adjust the JDK_ROOT variable in "compile.cmd".

- Run "compile.cmd".

- Commit "*.java" and "*.class" files to GIT.


To re-make the minimal JRE ("JRE-min.zip")
------------------------------------------

- (See: https://blog.adoptium.net/2021/10/jlink-to-produce-own-runtime/)

- If "*.class" are not made yet, recompile the "*.java" files as explained before.

- Adjust the JDK_ROOT variable in "deps.cmd" and "makejre.cmd".

- Run "deps.cmd". Notice the modules displayed in the last column (usually "java.base").

- Adjust the "--add-modules" argument in "makejre.cmd". It will be a comma-separated list of modules 
  from previous step (usually just "java.base").

- Delete the "JRE-min" folder if exists.

- Run "makejre.cmd". It will create a new "JRE-min" folder.

- Compress the "JRE-min" folder to "JRE-min.zip" file, uzing ZIP format, ultra level, Deflate or Deflate64 method.

- Commit "JRE-min.zip" to GIT.
